# The API. Left unset, the app talks to /api/v1 on its own origin, which is what
# the dev server proxies and what the production nginx serves.
# VITE_API_URL=https://api.example.com/api/v1

# The live feed, off unless all of these are set at build time.
#
# Without them the app refetches on its timer exactly as it did before: no
# socket is opened, nothing retries in the background, and nothing breaks. See
# backend/.env.example for the server half.
#
# The key is public by design — it identifies the application to the websocket
# server, and every channel is private and authorised through the API against
# the signed-in person. REVERB_APP_SECRET is the server's alone and must never
# appear here: anything in a VITE_ variable is compiled into the bundle a
# customer downloads.
# VITE_REVERB_APP_KEY=
# VITE_REVERB_HOST=ws.example.com
# VITE_REVERB_PORT=443
# VITE_REVERB_SCHEME=https

# Who runs the service, as the public pages (privacy, terms, data deletion, contact) state it.
# Public by nature — these are compiled into the bundle. Left unset, those pages show a visible
# "to be added before launch" marker; nothing is invented. Set them at build time.
# VITE_PUBLIC_LEGAL_NAME=
# VITE_PUBLIC_CONTACT_EMAIL=
# VITE_PUBLIC_ADDRESS=
# VITE_PUBLIC_PROCESSORS=
